Rāma mocks split mace and false tear-wiping boast --- Rāma vows Khara will sleep embracing bloody earth --- Rāma foretells fearless sages and scattering widows --- Khara retorts deathbound Rāma cannot tell right --- Khara uproots sāla tree and hurls it roaring --- Rāma shreds tree and pierces Khara with thousand shafts --- Rāma fells Khara with Indra-given Brahmadaṇḍa-like arrow --- Sages hail Rāma as Daṇḍaka protector by sage design --- Lakṣmaṇa and Sītā leave cave as Vaidēhī embraces Rāma